# PRs and git

- Branch per task: `agent/<short-task>`. Small PRs, one intent, < ~400 changed lines when possible.
- Conventional titles: `feat|fix|test|docs|refactor|chore|perf(scope): summary`.
- PR body sections (required): What · Why · How verified (exact commands + trimmed output) · Numbers changed (before → after + command) · Risks · Not done / follow-ups · Plan link (`.cursor/plans/...`) · Agent run link if any.
- Attach artifacts for anything visual or behavioral (screenshot, short video, eval table).
- Never force-push shared branches, rewrite history, tag, or publish. A human merges.
- The hook matcher includes `git pull` and `rebase`, so `git pull --rebase` reaches `.cursor/hooks/guard-shell.sh` and is denied. A plain `git pull` is allowed. Force-push is denied when `--force` or `-f` appears anywhere on `git push`, including after the remote. `git reset` is denied when `--hard` appears anywhere, including after the ref. `wget` piped to `bash` is denied the same way as `curl` piped to `bash`. A missing, blank, or non-string `command` is denied; invalid JSON exits non-zero.
- Address every Bugbot / Security Review finding: fix it or reply with a reason. Don't silently resolve.
